list.item:
Stroke-flavored properties (, ,
) route to , which prefers the
stroke slot when two-slot is engaged.

PreRender mirrors the runtime's Width / Height onto the stroke slot each
frame because the stroke is a plain renderable (not a layout-aware
) and won't auto-track its parent's size.

member.summary:
Renderable that receives the dropshadow each frame in . Prefer
fill when FillColor is set (so the shadow renders underneath any stroke layered on top);
otherwise fall back to stroke. Single-slot runtimes always pick the contained renderable.

The red channel (0-255) of the frame's per-frame color. Only applied when
 is ;
null (the identity, 255) if unset.

The top coordinate in texture coordinates of the AnimationFrame.  Default is 0.
This value is in texture coordinates, not pixels. A value of 1 represents the bottom
of the texture;

The bottom coordinate in texture coordinates of the AnimationFrame.  Default is 1.
This value is in texture coordinates, not pixels. A value of 1 represents the bottom
of the texture;
